# --- Corpus and artifacts (never committed; §6.3 release policy is code + manifest only)
# Leading slash matters: a bare `data/` also matches ravaan/data/ and configs/data/, which would
# silently drop the corpus pipeline source from the repo.
# Trailing `*` matters too: git cannot re-include a file whose *parent directory* is excluded,
# so `/data/` + `!/data/manifest.json` silently ignores the negation. `/data/*` excludes the
# entries rather than the directory, which is what makes the exceptions below work.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
!/data/manifest.json
/data/raw/
/checkpoints/
/runs/
/logs/
wandb/
*.arrow
*.parquet
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.zst
# ...except the ones under reports/, which are evidence rather than corpus. The stage-5
# validation sample is a .jsonl and the review sheet beside it is useless without it — the
# `score` command reads the metrics from here. Third time a blanket ignore has nearly dropped
# something load-bearing (session 2's bare `data/`, session 4's `/data/`), so: verified with
# `git check-ignore -v reports/quality_sample.jsonl`, which now reports nothing.
!/reports/*.jsonl
# Fourth instance, found session 17: the negation above is one level deep, so every measured-pair
# file under reports/freeze/ was silently ignored — including the two that Findings AA and AB were
# adjudicated from. They are ~30 KB each and they are the *only* record of which pairs the
# threshold decision was read against, which is precisely what `neardedup_threshold.md` says a
# threshold must be chosen from. Re-included explicitly.
!/reports/freeze/*.jsonl
# Detached-run console logs (`nohup … > reports/.decon_wiki.log`). Transient scratch, not evidence —
# the evidence is the JSON the run writes. Dot-prefixed so it cannot collide with a report name.
/reports/.*.log
*.txt.zst
*.model
*.vocab
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.npy

# --- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# --- Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build artifact for uploading the code to Kaggle/Colab; regenerate with git archive.
/ravaan-code.zip
# Google Drive's download bundles, when freeze results come back from a hosted run.
/ravaan-*T*Z-*.zip

# Freeze removal lists are evidence and are committed — Wikipedia's is 188 ids, and FineWeb2's
# will be smaller still (its self-similarity measured 9 clusters in 193,666 documents). Roman
# Urdu is the exception at 4,307,848 ids / 166 MB, which is corpus-scale rather than evidence-
# scale, so it follows §6.3's release policy instead: the statistics live in
# neardedup_roman.json and the file is pinned by removals_67_roman.sha256.json, both committed.
# It stays on disk — stages 9, 8 and 10 read it via --exclude — and is regenerable by re-running
# the 1.38 h pass. Named explicitly rather than globbed by size, because a rule that silently
# drops the *small* lists is the fourth instance of this file's recurring bug.
/reports/freeze/removals_67_roman.txt
